 "title": "The preimage of (1, 4) under x²",
 "caption": "The open interval (1, 4) on the y-axis pulls back to two open intervals, (−2, −1) and (1, 2): the points whose square lies strictly between 1 and 4. A union of open intervals is open, as continuity requires.",
 "alt": "The parabola y = x² with a horizontal band between y = 1 and y = 4, and the two x-intervals (−2, −1) and (1, 2) where the curve lies inside the band.",
 "description": [
  "Plot y = x² and mark the open interval (1, 4) on the y-axis.",
  "The curve is inside the band when 1 < x² < 4.",
  "That happens for x in (−2, −1) and for x in (1, 2).",
  "Both pieces are open intervals, so the preimage is open."
